Name: Collection folder (drive-letter root)
Id: collection-folder
Priority: 20
Provisional: false
Platform: windows             # modules for the other platform are left out of the plan for this target
Description: >
  A collection whose drive contents sit in a single drive-letter folder directly beneath
  the selection. VERIFIED against a real CyLR collection (2026-08-18):
  the drive folder is at the selection root, NOT nested under a hostname - CyLR names the
  zip after the host, it does not create a host folder. KAPE --tout produces the same shape.
Detect:
  Markers:
    - '?\Windows\System32\config\SYSTEM'
    - '?\$MFT'
  MatchMode: any
  DriveLetterFolder: true
Resolve:
  RootOffset: '?'
  Unescape: none
Notes: >
  Non-drive-letter siblings at the selection root are ignored, so a CyLR working directory
  containing CyLR.exe, CylR.log and the collection zip alongside C\ detects cleanly.
  Several drive-letter folders: GUI prompts; batch mode treats each as <Collection>_<Letter>.
